data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":631,"item_id":"msg_0048fb28b7388cc8016b03078dc6c887d1be51ed7262ba9130","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"birch-3\",\"decision\":\"reuse\",\"ability\":\"root-preparation\",\"reason\":\"The implemented stone-and-bark root preparation already provides a feasible version of the requested function: mechanically prepare owned roots with measurable changes and explicit costs. The three owned roots are suitable inputs, subject to their actual remaining freshness. Stone and bark must be obtained and validated; neither equipment nor mastery is supplied by this review. Cooking, detoxification and preservation are not necessary for these roots, whose recorded toxicity is zero, and are not effects of this method.\",\"specification\":\"Reuse root-preparation unchanged; individual learning requires 2 simulation rounds. Its public contract governs input references, quantities, progress and cancellation. Reserve one actual reusable stone and one actual reusable bark; process 1–4 owned roots at two working rounds per raw root and one energy per working round. Validate ownership, implement availability, interaction reach and the actual work location against shared geometry. Preserve input provenance, mass, nutrients, toxicity and accumulated spoilage rather than using the crushed-root resource's nominal zero nutrition as the meal's composition. Completed crushed roots age at 1.25 baseline: preparation is not preservation, sterilization or detoxification. Eating remains a separate eat operation, with actual nutrition, toxicity and spoilage checks; food does not directly heal. Track actual remaining work and partially processed food. Cancellation, including death, must release reserved implements and retain the actual food, processing fraction and age under the existing ownership/death rules, without duplicating or deleting escrow. No berries, heat source, vessel or new recipe is required for this equivalent method. Implementation and review advance no simulation time and grant no mastery.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Physical benefit comes from subsequently consuming the food's conserved nutrition, not from preparation itself; no extra calories, health or comfort are awarded. Do not add an alias satisfaction source. Retain the existing root-preparation practice rule only for qualified, paid, completed practice with genuinely changed outputs and a limited confirmed milestone—not requesting, study, mastery or every routine batch. Subscribe to practice-confirmed on root-preparation: the performing actor receives amount 0.4, cap 0.5, duration 8, refresh repetition and cooldown 12; maintained gain is 0.02 per qualifying event with decay 0.001. Actual eating emits meal-experience and uses the established meal feedback rules without inventing preparation enjoyment or label-only dietary diversity. Genuine experiments confirming new information may use the existing information-confirmed rule through probe, never an additional duplicate reward.\",\"visualReview\":\"Use the existing preparation presentation: display the actual reserved stone and bark, root quantity, working progress and resulting crushed food at the real work location. Bind food-preparation-started and food-preparation-completed to successful state transitions, and process-stopped to cancellation. Replay must represent paid work, retained partial processing and released implements faithfully; do not display cooking, steam, a constructed kitchen, extra food or a safety certification. Any wellbeing display must follow an actual qualified experience event, not learning or completion alone.\",\"learning\":2}]}","logprobs":[]}

